This shared library implements a client part of DICT protocol referenced by RFC 2229, excluding extensions.

The library uses glib, also you need cmake to build it. If you set -DGLIBDICTCLIENT_UTIL=ON, the utility program glib-dict-client will also be built. This program should be used only for testing the library.

To build:
cmake -S glibdictclient -B glibdictclient/build -DGLIBDICTCLIENT_UTIL=ON --preset release
cmake --build glibdictclient/build

To install:
cmake --install glibdictclient/build --prefix glibdictclient/install

To use:
compile your program with:
gcc -o /path/to/your/binary -Iglibdictclient/install/include -Lglibdictclient/install/lib64 /path/to/your/source.c

then run your program:
LD_LIBRARY_PATH="$LD_LIBRARY_PATH:glibdictclient/install/lib64" /path/to/your/binary

the same for the utility program:
LD_LIBRARY_PATH="$LD_LIBRARY_PATH:glibdictclient/install/lib64" glibdictclient/install/bin/glib-dict-client

To generate documentation for the library, use glibdictclient.doxy file (or your own one) in directory src:
cd glibdictclient/src && doxygen glibdictclient.doxy
